 "instruction": "A sweep over the cross-product of `PredictiveCodingLayer` mode flags (iPC steps × sparse gate × consolidation × learning gain, each run plainly, under gradient checkpointing, and under `freeze_plasticity`) turned up two real bugs. The incompatible-mode rules are also scattered across inline raises. Fix the bugs and centralize the rules.\n\n**Bug 1, iPC breaks backprop** (`luthi/v2/living_layer_pc.py`). With `inference_steps_per_forward > 1`, the inner loop rebinds `output` under `no_grad`, so the layer returns an activation with no gradient path. In a residual block the FFN branch then silently drops out of backward.\n- For T > 1, after the self-modify loop, recompute the returned output grad-capably as `x_flat @ self.weight.clone().T`, against the post-update weight.\n- T = 1 must stay bit-identical.\n\n**Bug 2, the NaN guard breaks gradient checkpointing.** The finiteness check on the grad-connected output makes autograd save the whole output. The recompute path skips that check, so non-reentrant checkpointing fails at backward with a saved-tensor count mismatch. Check `torch.isfinite(output.detach())` instead.\n\n**New module `luthi/v2/mode_compat.py`:**\n- `@dataclass(frozen=True) ModeIncompatibility` with fields `name`, `modes: tuple[str, ...]`, `enforced_at` and `reason`.\n- `INCOMPATIBILITIES` declares exactly these three rules:\n  - `\"ipc_x_grad_checkpoint\"`: iPC with T > 1 under a gradient-checkpoint recompute. Its reason must mention `iPC`.\n  - `\"recompute_without_original\"`: a checkpoint replay reaches the layer but no weight snapshot was cached by an original forward. That happens when the original ran under `freeze_plasticity()`, or `clear_forward_cache()` ran before backward.\n  - `\"lived_reencode_x_grad_checkpoint\"`: the lived JEPA re-encode with encoder gradient checkpointing (the existing raise in `JEPALoss.compute_lived_loss`).\n- `get_rule(name)` looks a rule up by name and raises `KeyError` for an undeclared one.\n- `raise_incompatible(name, extra=\"\")` raises `RuntimeError(f\"Incompatible modes {' x '.join(modes)}: {reason}\")`, with ` [extra]` appended when `extra` is given.\n- Export all four names.\n\n**Route the existing raises through it:**\n- The iPC-under-recompute check in the layer passes `extra` with the T value.\n- The lived-re-encode check is in `jepa_loss.py`.\n- **New check:** in the layer's recompute branch, read the cached `_fwd_weight_snapshot` and `_fwd_episode_delta` with `getattr(..., None)`. Raise `recompute_without_original` when there is no snapshot, instead of failing cryptically or reusing a stale one.\n\n**Required behavior across the matrix:**\n- Outputs are finite.\n- Buffers change only on the live path.\n- Checkpointed runs are bit-identical to plain runs in output, gradients and buffers.\n- Frozen runs change nothing.\n- The three forbidden cells raise errors starting `Incompatible modes`.",
